                        "entry_id": "86e1a698-55eb-3d73-a5ba-373e91591995",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Beaked: having a beak."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "310fc268-7b1d-42b0-88f8-07e628825323",
                                "sense_id": "09df8616-19c0-3f65-8118-11ee8d7eb66a",
                                "text": "Jim Carrey tells John Hiscock about his beaky new co-stars in 'Mr Popper's Penguins' and how he made it big."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d8250847-442f-32f5-aa8f-376674326336",
                        "entry_id": "86e1a698-55eb-3d73-a5ba-373e91591995",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Beak-like: resembling a beak."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1a3b3942-c1d3-4501-bfa9-1b286798b186",
                                "sense_id": "d8250847-442f-32f5-aa8f-376674326336",
                                "text": "beaky nose"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bdfeb6e8-b0ef-4457-8788-849f430ab89d",
                                "sense_id": "d8250847-442f-32f5-aa8f-376674326336",
                                "text": "[…] Hector thunder'd threats aloud,\nAnd rush'd enraged before the Trojan crowd;\nThen swift invades the ships, whose beaky prores\nLay rank'd contiguous on the bending shores;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0e1f77f7-b104-45da-aa2e-9ac2effade5d",
                                "sense_id": "d8250847-442f-32f5-aa8f-376674326336",
                                "text": "[…] he emerged from the signals room with his drooping mustache, his beaky nose, his stupid, staring eyes […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7543faa4-19c3-3730-9546-2155eb0b5254",
                        "entry_id": "86e1a698-55eb-3d73-a5ba-373e91591995",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having a nose which resembles a beak."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7fdf5f43-ea7e-40c8-ac42-4084878e9c3a",
                                "sense_id": "7543faa4-19c3-3730-9546-2155eb0b5254",
                                "text": "beaky face"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2511d93b-4809-4ab4-8d24-04db6eb52ec5",
                                "sense_id": "7543faa4-19c3-3730-9546-2155eb0b5254",
                                "text": "\"[…] You haven't a nose like mine. I'll be as beaky as Father in ten more years. […]\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e0bb2c01-c1f6-484a-a9e8-fe86aa6617ef",
                                "sense_id": "7543faa4-19c3-3730-9546-2155eb0b5254",
                                "text": "The two men, who for more than sixty years had never been very much out of touch, were quite similar in appearance: spare of form, with beaky, weathered faces and strands of whitening hair."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "68ffd61f-e166-3a3f-8430-8bff7cc88c9f",
                        "entry_id": "86e1a698-55eb-3d73-a5ba-373e91591995",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Made using a beak; (of a sound) produced through a beak. (of a gesture)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4528f951-c04a-444c-8b91-d513ec606a3d",
                                "sense_id": "68ffd61f-e166-3a3f-8430-8bff7cc88c9f",
                                "text": "1929, D. H. Lawrence, The Escaped Cock, published as The Man Who Died, London: Heinemann, 1931, pp. 34-35, http://gutenberg.net.au/ebooks07/0700631h.html\nAnd always the man who had died saw not the bird alone, but the short, sharp wave of life of which the bird was the crest. He watched the queer, beaky motion of the creature as it gobbled into itself the scraps of food; its glancing of the eye of life, ever alert and watchful […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "da269561-9d27-45bb-ac30-d23fb327ed85",
                                "sense_id": "68ffd61f-e166-3a3f-8430-8bff7cc88c9f",
                                "text": "If you put your hand on [the hens], they flattened their feathers to their bodies and their bodies down on their eggs and gave beaky growls."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
